00:20:37,276 --> 00:20:39,949
From a risk-management standpoint,

256
00:20:39,949 --> 00:20:43,173
accepting her resignation
is the quickest solution.

257
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:49,791
But if you plan to keep Ms. Nam,
we can pursue defamatory comments

258
00:20:49,791 --> 00:20:52,310
under the Information
and Communications Network Act.

259
00:20:52,310 --> 00:20:56,330
And we can go after the protesters
for interfering with business.

260
00:20:58,549 --> 00:21:00,846
So even if we win legally,

261
00:21:00,846 --> 00:21:04,042
public opinion of APPELLO could get even worse.

262
00:21:04,042 --> 00:21:06,182
Most likely.

263
00:21:12,236 --> 00:21:14,179
They gave us a ton of vongole.

264
00:21:14,179 --> 00:21:17,473
Yeah. This looks really good.

265
00:21:17,473 --> 00:21:18,953
Yeah.

266
00:21:24,689 --> 00:21:26,632
- Hey, you saw that earlier, huh?
- Yeah, yeah.

267
00:21:26,632 --> 00:21:30,160
Her CEO pulled her in like this
and took the egg for her.

268
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,990
"Stop right now!"

269
00:21:31,990 --> 00:21:33,537
That was so freaking cool.

270
00:21:33,537 --> 00:21:36,396
- My heart skipped a beat.
- Exactly!

271
00:21:45,329 --> 00:21:46,716
Focus on your food.

272
00:21:46,716 --> 00:21:48,528
No overthinking.

273
00:21:50,069 --> 00:21:51,422
Here.

274
00:21:52,737 --> 00:21:54,874
Do I look...

275
00:21:54,874 --> 00:21:58,967
like a sasaeng fan to you too?

276
00:22:01,853 --> 00:22:03,070
Da Reum.

277
00:22:03,070 --> 00:22:05,276
I was his fan...

278
00:22:06,551 --> 00:22:09,077
and I even joined his company.

279
00:22:10,884 --> 00:22:14,177
Anyone could get the wrong idea.

280
00:22:14,177 --> 00:22:17,048
CEO Kang probably thinks that too.

281
00:22:17,048 --> 00:22:18,374
Come on.

282
00:22:18,374 --> 00:22:19,491
Well...

283
00:22:19,491 --> 00:22:22,091
Everyone keeps calling me a sasaeng.

284
00:22:22,091 --> 00:22:26,480
It feels like all those years
I loved him have been tainted.

285
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:27,765
Why would you say that?

286
00:22:27,765 --> 00:22:32,119
Whatever people say, that's not who you are.

287
00:22:32,119 --> 00:22:36,286
By that logic,
fans aren't allowed to get jobs now?

288
00:22:36,286 --> 00:22:40,146
You worked hard
and got into the company you wanted!

289
00:22:40,146 --> 00:22:42,932
How is that a crime?

290
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:07,316
[Celebrity Community]

291
00:23:07,316 --> 00:23:08,909
What?

292
00:23:13,221 --> 00:23:15,559
[Blurry, but I got the sasaeng on camera]

293
00:23:15,559 --> 00:23:17,000
[Restricted due to
a rights infringement report]

294
00:23:24,478 --> 00:23:27,104
Thank goodness.

295
00:23:27,104 --> 00:23:30,191
But who reported the post?

296
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:37,861
Nice to flex my legal muscles again.

297
00:23:37,861 --> 00:23:39,797
Good work.

298
00:23:39,797 --> 00:23:42,047
But...

299
00:23:42,047 --> 00:23:45,060
Do you really have to go this far?

300
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:46,258
What?

301
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:49,921
Do you have to be this ruthless?

302
00:23:55,458 --> 00:23:56,711
Hey...

303
00:23:58,776 --> 00:24:00,335
Man...

304
00:24:11,940 --> 00:24:13,670
Hey.

305
00:24:13,670 --> 00:24:17,166
Do you know how much hell you put us through?

306
00:24:18,829 --> 00:24:20,829
We need to talk.

307
00:24:24,182 --> 00:24:26,888
We'll talk later.

308
00:24:40,096 --> 00:24:41,752
How's Da Reum?

309
00:24:47,025 --> 00:24:48,965
"Da Reum?"

310
00:24:49,638 --> 00:24:52,625
You're not even hiding it now.

311
00:24:54,952 --> 00:24:56,502
Was she okay at work today?

312
00:24:56,502 --> 00:24:58,935
You're a director here!
Do you have no sense of responsibility?

313
00:24:58,935 --> 00:25:01,448
Look what happened to APPELLO.

314
00:25:03,034 --> 00:25:06,661
I'm sorry. A correction will be out soon.

315
00:25:07,868 --> 00:25:10,461
You think saying sorry is enough?

316
00:25:13,402 --> 00:25:16,241
What about everyone who depends on APPELLO?

317
00:25:16,867 --> 00:25:18,238
Did you think about them?

318
00:25:18,238 --> 00:25:20,738
Da Reum and I...

319
00:25:22,138 --> 00:25:23,969
aren't dating.

320
00:25:23,969 --> 00:25:26,281
And she's definitely not a sasaeng fan.

321
00:25:26,281 --> 00:25:28,158
I don't want you to misunderstand.

322
00:25:28,158 --> 00:25:31,172
Look what you've already done!

323
00:25:31,172 --> 00:25:34,653
APPELLO lost trust overnight.
Da Reum's been torn apart.

324
00:25:34,653 --> 00:25:37,539
They've branded her a sasaeng fan!

325
00:25:40,453 --> 00:25:45,499
You should've at least told me.

326
00:25:49,505 --> 00:25:50,986
What about you?

327
00:25:52,665 --> 00:25:54,775
Do you tell me everything?

328
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:04,954
I heard about your mom's accident
from someone else.

329
00:26:06,943 --> 00:26:09,116
And what about Jeong Yeon?

330
00:26:10,544 --> 00:26:14,816
When I asked how you felt about Da Reum,
were you honest with me?

331
00:26:15,830 --> 00:26:17,199
Hey.

332
00:26:20,390 --> 00:26:23,170
Do you even think of me as a friend?

333
00:26:32,689 --> 00:26:35,601
If the investors push for it, I'll step down.

334
00:26:35,601 --> 00:26:37,896
I'll take responsibility.

335
00:26:42,362 --> 00:26:43,996
"Responsibility?"

336
00:26:44,652 --> 00:26:47,465
Then put out the fire you started.

337
00:26:50,681 --> 00:26:52,411
[Protect Lee Chan]
Boycott APPELLO!

338
00:26:52,411 --> 00:26:54,124
- Boycott! Boycott!
- Boycott! Boycott!

339
00:26:54,124 --> 00:26:55,774
A sasaeng employee? Shame on you!

340
00:26:55,774 --> 00:26:57,481
- Shame on you! Shame on you!
- Shame on you! Shame on you!

341
00:26:57,481 --> 00:26:59,291
Boycott APPELLO!

342
00:26:59,291 --> 00:27:01,097
- Boycott! Boycott!
- Boycott! Boycott!

343
00:27:01,697 --> 00:27:05,798
Does Director Lee have any sense at all?

344
00:27:05,798 --> 00:27:09,622
SE Trading is pushing hard
to launch its own fashion platform,

345
00:27:09,622 --> 00:27:11,360
and now there's a boycott?

346
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:12,692
Yes, I understand.

347
00:27:12,692 --> 00:27:16,105
I know you are concerned,
but please give us a little time.

348
00:27:16,105 --> 00:27:18,075
Things have started to calm down...

349
00:27:18,075 --> 00:27:20,935
"Calm down?" It's chaos outside!

350
00:27:20,935 --> 00:27:23,395
How can one employee put our valuation at risk?

351
00:27:23,395 --> 00:27:28,475
If that employee is a real risk,
then let her go!

352
00:27:28,475 --> 00:27:30,345
- Exactly.
- Hold on.

353
00:27:30,345 --> 00:27:35,016
So we cave to public pressure
even when it's not true?

354
00:27:35,016 --> 00:27:36,642
The customer is always right.

355
00:27:36,642 --> 00:27:39,639
If customers are upset,
you apologize and keep your head down.

356
00:27:39,639 --> 00:27:41,526
What? That's not right.

357
00:27:41,526 --> 00:27:43,130
We've already issued a correction...

358
00:27:43,130 --> 00:27:45,036
Hold on! Don't get worked up!

359
00:27:49,516 --> 00:27:52,234
Maybe this dies down for now.

360
00:27:52,234 --> 00:27:54,234
But what happens next time?

361
00:28:00,595 --> 00:28:03,280
If we cave every time this happens,

362
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:05,184
we'll end up sacrificing
someone even more important.

363
00:28:05,184 --> 00:28:06,276
CEO Kang.

364
00:28:06,276 --> 00:28:08,589
This isn't the time for ideals.

365
00:28:08,589 --> 00:28:10,869
I'm talking about principles.

366
00:28:10,869 --> 00:28:14,453
Ms. Nam has proven herself
to be a valuable employee.

367
00:28:14,453 --> 00:28:18,613
Shouldn't we treat this
as a management issue, not a personal one?

368
00:28:21,173 --> 00:28:25,923
Whatever we decide, I'll take responsibility.

369
00:28:28,276 --> 00:28:32,673
I run APPELLO,
and my track record speaks for itself.

370
00:28:32,673 --> 00:28:34,063
Fine.

371
00:28:34,063 --> 00:28:37,070
Then the SE platform launch
will be the real test.

372
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:39,684
We'll see if you can keep that seat.

373
00:28:42,116 --> 00:28:46,036
The results will speak for themselves.

374
00:28:55,608 --> 00:28:57,367
CEO Kang.

375
00:29:06,255 --> 00:29:08,371
Are you sure about this?

376
00:29:08,371 --> 00:29:10,258
About what?

377
00:29:10,258 --> 00:29:14,236
I think I know what choice you just made.

378
00:29:15,116 --> 00:29:16,691
Then back me up.

379
00:29:16,691 --> 00:29:18,764
CEO Kang.

380
00:29:18,764 --> 00:29:21,501
As your employee, I will.

381
00:29:21,501 --> 00:29:23,072
But...

382
00:29:23,072 --> 00:29:26,167
As someone like a brother to you,
I have to say this.

383
00:29:26,167 --> 00:29:31,073
Ha Gi, keep this up
and you could lose your job as CEO.

384
00:29:35,965 --> 00:29:38,223
I'll see everyone out.

385
00:29:56,159 --> 00:29:58,296
There's still a lot to handle.

386
00:29:58,296 --> 00:30:00,949
[Space Layout]
I wonder if everything's going okay.

387
00:30:05,196 --> 00:30:07,086
Then again...

388
00:30:07,086 --> 00:30:10,165
The company won't fall apart
just because I'm gone.

389
00:30:21,202 --> 00:30:22,336
[Master Im Cheong Rim]

390
00:30:23,320 --> 00:30:25,143
Hello, Master Im.

391
00:30:25,143 --> 00:30:26,747
Yes, Ms. Nam.

392
00:30:26,747 --> 00:30:28,411
This is Im Cheong Rim.

393
00:30:28,411 --> 00:30:30,455
Yes, go ahead.

394
00:30:30,455 --> 00:30:33,264
How are the event preparations going?

395
00:30:36,129 --> 00:30:37,273
Of course.

396
00:30:37,273 --> 00:30:40,410
I'm right in the middle of it.

397
00:30:40,410 --> 00:30:41,980
[Nam Da Reum]

398
00:30:41,980 --> 00:30:45,027
<i>Did you get the proposal and samples I sent?</i>

399
00:30:45,027 --> 00:30:46,460
Well...

400
00:30:46,460 --> 00:30:49,070
They weren't bad.

401
00:30:49,070 --> 00:30:51,923
She really likes both Lee Chan and the event.

402
00:30:51,923 --> 00:30:53,390
Oh, stop.

403
00:30:53,390 --> 00:30:55,320
<i>Anyway...</i>

404
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:58,720
<i>I had a few notes, so I emailed you.</i>

405
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:00,863
I'll be in Seoul in a few days.

406
00:31:00,863 --> 00:31:02,676
We can go over everything then.

407
00:31:03,643 --> 00:31:05,681
Okay. I'll check it.

408
00:31:05,681 --> 00:31:08,540
Yes. Take care.

409
00:31:15,458 --> 00:31:17,891
What am I going to do?

410
00:31:19,338 --> 00:31:21,329
Get it together, Nam Da Reum.

411
00:31:21,329 --> 00:31:22,948
This is no time to fall apart.

412
00:31:25,773 --> 00:31:28,340
[Subject: APPELLO Showroom Revision Request]

413
00:31:28,340 --> 00:31:29,343
[Download complete]

414
00:31:35,095 --> 00:31:36,438
Yes.

415
00:31:37,589 --> 00:31:38,846
Sir.

416
00:31:38,846 --> 00:31:42,695
It looks like Master Im sent feedback.

417
00:31:44,081 --> 00:31:48,078
Da Reum organized her notes and sent them over.

418
00:31:48,078 --> 00:31:50,874
You should check your email.

419
00:31:51,827 --> 00:31:54,258
- Okay.
- Okay.

420
00:32:03,848 --> 00:32:05,793
[This is Nam Da Reum from Marketing]

421
00:32:11,213 --> 00:32:12,843
[Knot Showroom Pop-Up Revision Report]

422
00:32:12,843 --> 00:32:14,483
[Nam Da Reum]

423
00:32:19,021 --> 00:32:20,855
[APPELLO Showroom Top View
Updated with Master Im's Revisions]

424
00:32:22,915 --> 00:32:24,579
<i>Let's do it together, sir!</i>

425
00:32:24,579 --> 00:32:26,660
<i>When things get tough, you have to smile more.</i>

426
00:32:26,660 --> 00:32:31,403
<i>If you keep smiling,
you really do start to feel better.</i>

427
00:32:38,558 --> 00:32:40,281
<i>But Mom...</i>

428
00:32:40,281 --> 00:32:43,208
<i>Even though it's a small company,</i>

429
00:32:43,208 --> 00:32:49,615
<i>it's a place where my ideas matter
and I have a voice.</i>

430
00:32:49,615 --> 00:32:52,448
<i>That's why I love APPELLO...</i>

431
00:32:53,695 --> 00:32:56,214
<i>and I'm much happier here.</i>

432
00:32:59,072 --> 00:33:03,659
<i>I don't want to hurt the company.</i>

433
00:34:01,551 --> 00:34:05,414
The office feels so empty without Da Reum.

434
00:34:05,414 --> 00:34:08,681
She was our ray of sunshine.

435
00:34:08,681 --> 00:34:10,467
Exactly.

436
00:34:11,337 --> 00:34:14,642
I really miss her.

437
00:34:14,642 --> 00:34:18,510
And lately,
it looked like she wasn't eating much.

438
00:34:19,193 --> 00:34:22,110
I hope she's okay.

439
00:34:22,110 --> 00:34:24,545
We've got the event to worry about first.

440
00:34:24,545 --> 00:34:27,470
I honestly have no idea what to do.

441
00:34:27,470 --> 00:34:31,149
I really have no idea either.

442
00:34:32,979 --> 00:34:37,872
Should we send her an SOS?

443
00:34:39,146 --> 00:34:41,002
Think we should?

444
00:34:41,002 --> 00:34:42,725
Let's do it.

445
00:35:03,115 --> 00:35:06,658
<i>Go see reporter Do Eun Yeong,
who broke the story.</i>

446
00:35:06,658 --> 00:35:08,258
<i>You can handle that much, right?</i>

447
00:35:13,023 --> 00:35:14,062
Yes.

448
00:35:14,062 --> 00:35:17,115
The massage was amazing today.

449
00:35:17,115 --> 00:35:19,185
No need to thank me.

450
00:35:19,185 --> 00:35:22,138
I should be thanking you for that dating scoop.

451
00:35:22,138 --> 00:35:23,420
And...

452
00:35:26,088 --> 00:35:28,995
I'll call you back in a bit.

453
00:35:31,255 --> 00:35:32,905
I read your article.

454
00:35:32,905 --> 00:35:34,491
Reporter Do.

455
00:35:35,192 --> 00:35:37,731
Doesn't Cho Yi come here too?

456
00:35:38,422 --> 00:35:40,679
You must be doing pretty well.

457
00:35:40,679 --> 00:35:45,519
A luxury members-only spa,
all the latest designer goods...

458
00:35:51,884 --> 00:35:54,463
Looks like you've done your homework.

459
00:35:56,420 --> 00:35:58,471
You know...

460
00:35:58,471 --> 00:36:03,032
You don't land this many exclusives
unless you're pretty close.

461
00:36:03,032 --> 00:36:04,053
So?

462
00:36:05,645 --> 00:36:07,009
Why are you here?

463
00:36:07,009 --> 00:36:09,075
Run a correction.

464
00:36:12,824 --> 00:36:14,887
She's not a sasaeng fan.

465
00:36:14,887 --> 00:36:18,636
Corrections are for factual errors.

466
00:36:18,636 --> 00:36:20,800
That's exactly what this is.

467
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:23,073
I came to tell you myself.

468
00:36:26,261 --> 00:36:28,440
And if I refuse?

469
00:36:29,121 --> 00:36:31,711
Then I have a tip of my own.

470
00:36:31,711 --> 00:36:34,548
All those luxury spa treatments
and designer gifts

471
00:36:34,548 --> 00:36:38,384
you've been getting since the article ran.

472
00:36:38,384 --> 00:36:39,877
Something like this?

473
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:47,512
Are you threatening the press?

474
00:36:47,512 --> 00:36:49,923
I'm an actor.

475
00:36:49,923 --> 00:36:53,329
If I speak up, it'll make waves.

476
00:36:55,966 --> 00:36:59,539
I can soften the article.

477
00:36:59,539 --> 00:37:00,949
I'll take out "sasaeng."

478
00:37:00,949 --> 00:37:06,125
I'm asking for a correction, not a rewrite.

479
00:37:20,817 --> 00:37:21,841
[Express Delivery]

480
00:37:21,841 --> 00:37:23,045
[Delivery Riders Wanted]

481
00:37:25,844 --> 00:37:28,492
He must've come through here at least once.

482
00:37:41,590 --> 00:37:44,867
Why is nobody showing up today?

483
00:37:44,867 --> 00:37:47,219
I've got orders piling up.

484
00:37:48,133 --> 00:37:49,163
Oh, man...

485
00:37:49,163 --> 00:37:50,909
This is the place, right?

486
00:37:50,909 --> 00:37:52,092
Yeah, that's right.

487
00:37:52,092 --> 00:37:54,710
I'm starving. I don't even have time to eat!

488
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:55,754
Go, hurry!

489
00:37:55,754 --> 00:37:57,370
Darn it.

490
00:37:58,452 --> 00:38:00,352
Oh my gosh...

491
00:38:00,946 --> 00:38:03,552
Excuse me, sir.

492
00:38:03,552 --> 00:38:05,822
Do you happen to have a delivery rider who...

493
00:38:05,822 --> 00:38:08,322
- Why are you so late?
- Sorry?

494
00:38:08,322 --> 00:38:09,680
Perfect timing.

495
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:11,896
You've got a helmet and a bike!

496
00:38:11,896 --> 00:38:15,113
My bike's just parked out front for a minute...

497
00:38:15,113 --> 00:38:17,243
A bike can handle this one.

498
00:38:17,243 --> 00:38:19,144
- It's nearby.
- No, wait.

499
00:38:19,144 --> 00:38:21,283
- It's fine.
- I'm not... No, no.

500
00:38:21,283 --> 00:38:23,573
- That's not why I'm here, sir.
- You're fine.

501
00:38:23,573 --> 00:38:24,903
- I just...
- By the intersection...

502
00:38:24,903 --> 00:38:26,103
What?

503
00:38:26,103 --> 00:38:27,123
Fiery Chicken Feet!

504
00:38:27,123 --> 00:38:29,574
It's an urgent order. Get going, okay?

505
00:38:29,574 --> 00:38:31,412
Wait. I didn't come for a delivery.

506
00:38:31,412 --> 00:38:33,138
- I'm looking for someone...
- Got it, got it.

507
00:38:33,138 --> 00:38:34,689
- I'm here to find someone.
- Got it.

508
00:38:34,689 --> 00:38:37,056
- Could you just listen for one second?
- Let's go.

509
00:38:37,056 --> 00:38:39,656
I won't even charge you commission for a while.

510
00:38:39,656 --> 00:38:40,842
Please!

511
00:38:40,842 --> 00:38:42,979
No, wait...

512
00:38:42,979 --> 00:38:44,575
Sir...

513
00:38:49,823 --> 00:38:51,444
[Takeout Available]

514
00:38:52,731 --> 00:38:54,511
Bye.

515
00:38:58,026 --> 00:39:01,372
If he won't show up, I'll find him myself.

516
00:39:03,849 --> 00:39:07,779
Roy,
if you won't come to me, I'm coming to you.

517
00:39:07,779 --> 00:39:09,892
Just wait!

518
00:39:51,969 --> 00:39:53,874
[Fire the sasaeng fan now!]

519
00:40:13,497 --> 00:40:15,450
Now it really feels like...

520
00:40:16,824 --> 00:40:19,250
I shouldn't be here.

521
00:40:29,259 --> 00:40:31,118
[APPELLO Values a Sasaeng
Over Lee Chan's Safety]

522
00:40:31,118 --> 00:40:32,472
[Lee Chan Protection Alliance]

523
00:40:54,756 --> 00:40:57,422
Don't say a word from now on.

524
00:40:58,136 --> 00:40:59,367
Min Ah...

525
00:40:59,367 --> 00:41:01,173
Don't say anything!

526
00:41:01,173 --> 00:41:02,720
What?

527
00:41:04,372 --> 00:41:05,528
Oh my!

528
00:41:05,528 --> 00:41:07,895
What's going on?

529
00:41:07,895 --> 00:41:09,214
Ta-da!

530
00:41:10,307 --> 00:41:13,072
Da Reum, we missed you so much.

531
00:41:13,072 --> 00:41:15,429
We were so worried about you.

532
00:41:15,429 --> 00:41:18,695
I missed you too!

533
00:41:20,716 --> 00:41:23,867
I've been worried about this too.

534
00:41:23,867 --> 00:41:27,262
Let me show you Master Im's requests
and the new layout.

535
00:41:27,262 --> 00:41:31,267
I redesigned it with her revisions...

536
00:41:31,267 --> 00:41:32,885
Especially...

537
00:41:32,885 --> 00:41:34,994
This demonstration area here...

538
00:41:34,994 --> 00:41:36,825
Da Reum...

539
00:41:36,825 --> 00:41:40,064
Why are you still worrying
about work right now?

540
00:41:40,064 --> 00:41:42,484
What about you?

541
00:41:44,397 --> 00:41:47,274
After being home for a few days...

542
00:41:47,274 --> 00:41:52,777
I realized how happy I was
just waking up and going to work.

543
00:41:52,777 --> 00:41:56,324
I can't stop thinking about the event.

544
00:41:56,324 --> 00:41:58,324
Classic Nam Da Reum.

545
00:42:02,830 --> 00:42:06,521
How's CEO Kang doing?

546
00:42:06,521 --> 00:42:10,151
He barely says a word these days.

547
00:42:10,151 --> 00:42:12,709
He just works even harder.

548
00:42:12,709 --> 00:42:15,502
I have no idea what he's thinking.

549
00:43:41,283 --> 00:43:43,283
Why am I here?

550
00:43:50,724 --> 00:43:52,537
Sir?

551
00:43:59,955 --> 00:44:03,169
What are you doing here?

552
00:44:05,170 --> 00:44:06,950
Oh, well...

553
00:44:12,099 --> 00:44:14,458
I was on my way home.

554
00:44:16,190 --> 00:44:18,693
This way?

555
00:44:18,693 --> 00:44:20,773
Yeah, kind of.

556
00:44:23,176 --> 00:44:25,447
We live in the same neighborhood.

557
00:44:25,447 --> 00:44:27,623
We could just run into each other...

558
00:44:27,623 --> 00:44:29,449
Anyway...

559
00:44:30,436 --> 00:44:32,165
I was passing by.

560
00:44:35,836 --> 00:44:38,822
Have you been well?

561
00:44:40,323 --> 00:44:42,269
Yeah, more or less.

562
00:44:45,533 --> 00:44:47,497
And you?

563
00:44:47,497 --> 00:44:49,497
Have you been okay?

564
00:44:53,881 --> 00:44:55,647
No.

565
00:45:01,461 --> 00:45:05,291
If you came to see me...

566
00:45:05,291 --> 00:45:07,851
you can just say so, sir.

567
00:45:08,825 --> 00:45:10,903
Say what?

568
00:45:10,903 --> 00:45:13,690
I won't resent you if you fire me.

569
00:45:13,690 --> 00:45:16,681
I resigned because
I wanted to take responsibility.

570
00:45:16,681 --> 00:45:20,426
- The company should issue a statement...
- What are you talking about?

571
00:45:24,893 --> 00:45:29,233
I've had some time to sort things out.

572
00:45:33,482 --> 00:45:35,098
I'm fine.

573
00:45:35,098 --> 00:45:38,037
You're never fine. Why do you keep saying that?

574
00:45:38,037 --> 00:45:40,527
With that look on your face?

575
00:45:40,527 --> 00:45:42,957
That's what you came to tell me anyway.

576
00:45:42,957 --> 00:45:44,685
I came because I missed you.

577
00:45:44,685 --> 00:45:47,534
I was worried about you. Is that enough?

578
00:46:09,020 --> 00:46:11,886
It's late, so...

579
00:46:15,386 --> 00:46:17,319
Go inside.

580
00:46:17,951 --> 00:46:19,899
Good night.

581
00:46:38,105 --> 00:46:40,864
He came because he missed me?

582
00:47:17,371 --> 00:47:19,415
[Jan 22, 2026]
[CEO Kang came to my house]

583
00:47:25,489 --> 00:47:26,743
[Finally! My first day at APPELLO!]

584
00:47:28,502 --> 00:47:30,748
[Best Employee Project]
[Appointed CEO Kang's secret agent]

585
00:47:30,748 --> 00:47:32,820
[Get on CEO Kang's good side!]
[Avoid CEO Kang!]

586
00:47:33,980 --> 00:47:35,191
[CEO Kang]

587
00:47:35,191 --> 00:47:36,484
[CEO Kang]

588
00:47:36,484 --> 00:47:37,573
[CEO Kang]

589
00:47:39,176 --> 00:47:42,350
[CEO Kang]

590
00:47:43,644 --> 00:47:46,644
[CEO Kang]

591
00:47:50,147 --> 00:47:52,292
[I keep thinking about CEO Kang]

592
00:47:52,292 --> 00:47:55,058
[What did he mean?]
[I don't know! I'm so confused]

593
00:47:59,697 --> 00:48:01,600
What...

594
00:48:01,600 --> 00:48:05,061
Why is everything I wrote about him?

595
00:48:25,036 --> 00:48:28,700
<i>Sir, why are you so serious
about this claw machine?</i>

596
00:48:28,700 --> 00:48:30,670
<i>A goal has been set.</i>

597
00:48:30,670 --> 00:48:31,724
<i>I have to get Pong.</i>

598
00:48:31,724 --> 00:48:35,885
<i>Even though Ping and Pong are gone,
you can still contact me.</i>

599
00:48:37,193 --> 00:48:38,979
<i>For no reason at all.</i>

600
00:48:45,305 --> 00:48:47,691
What's wrong with me?

601
00:49:15,553 --> 00:49:19,537
Reporter Do won't be coming.

602
00:49:19,537 --> 00:49:22,070
I gave her a bigger story.

603
00:49:26,280 --> 00:49:28,280
Cho Yi.

604
00:49:28,867 --> 00:49:31,621
Don't cross the line again.

605
00:49:31,621 --> 00:49:33,257
That's why I came.

606
00:49:33,257 --> 00:49:34,973
What?

607
00:49:38,369 --> 00:49:44,224
Go after her one more time,
and I won't let it slide.

608
00:49:47,708 --> 00:49:49,534
So?

609
00:49:50,981 --> 00:49:55,125
You're doing all this just to protect her?

610
00:49:55,125 --> 00:49:58,560
Oppa, get a grip.

611
00:49:58,560 --> 00:50:01,146
Do you know how bad this makes you look?

612
00:50:01,146 --> 00:50:03,519
If the dating rumor had been about us...

613
00:50:03,519 --> 00:50:08,217
Sure, some people would've been jealous,
but they'd say we made sense together.

614
00:50:08,217 --> 00:50:09,587
But with her?

615
00:50:09,587 --> 00:50:12,413
People just judge you for it.

616
00:50:12,413 --> 00:50:14,643
- Hey, Yun Cho Yi.
- I told you.

617
00:50:14,643 --> 00:50:17,536
People should be with someone on their level.

618
00:50:17,536 --> 00:50:21,298
You two only drag each other down.

619
00:50:21,298 --> 00:50:23,044
Don't you get it?

620
00:50:29,506 --> 00:50:31,832
I'll deal with the fallout.

621
00:50:32,463 --> 00:50:34,542
And I'll make my own choices.

622
00:50:35,602 --> 00:50:38,316
Stay away from Da Reum.

623
00:50:38,316 --> 00:50:40,589
This is your last warning.

624
00:50:48,591 --> 00:50:50,595
Hey.

625
00:50:50,595 --> 00:50:52,581
Lee Chan!

626
00:50:58,921 --> 00:51:01,112
Lee Chan is here with us today.

627
00:51:01,112 --> 00:51:03,357
Thank you for this exclusive interview.

628
00:51:03,357 --> 00:51:04,401
Of course.

629
00:51:04,401 --> 00:51:08,307
First, we'd like to hear
your thoughts on the recent controversy.

630
00:51:11,078 --> 00:51:13,668
As a public figure, I know I fell short.

631
00:51:13,668 --> 00:51:19,058
She is not a sasaeng fan.

632
00:51:19,058 --> 00:51:23,541
She's a fan who supports me,
just like any other, and a colleague.

633
00:51:23,541 --> 00:51:27,217
Nothing more, nothing less?

634
00:51:28,091 --> 00:51:29,373
That's right.

635
00:51:30,618 --> 00:51:36,126
I don't think liking someone
should ever be a reason for criticism.

636
00:51:37,364 --> 00:51:42,511
I'd also ask that people stop attacking her.

637
00:51:43,171 --> 00:51:46,011
Any words for your fans?

638
00:51:52,324 --> 00:51:55,257
I'm sorry, and thank you.

639
00:51:56,358 --> 00:52:01,204
I treasure all the time
you've spent supporting me.

640
00:52:01,918 --> 00:52:05,971
Your support is what got me this far.

641
00:52:13,261 --> 00:52:16,194
I hope we can keep supporting each other

642
00:52:16,988 --> 00:52:19,801
and stay together for a long time.

643
00:52:29,270 --> 00:52:32,974
[Knot]

644
00:52:38,653 --> 00:52:40,790
Just as you requested,

645
00:52:40,790 --> 00:52:44,784
we set up the exhibit, story,
and experience zones.

646
00:52:44,784 --> 00:52:47,944
We also revised the activity kits.

647
00:52:47,944 --> 00:52:53,466
The layout shows how APPELLO
carries your tradition forward.

648
00:52:58,720 --> 00:53:00,677
Where's Ms. Nam?

649
00:53:02,920 --> 00:53:06,423
She's off today.

650
00:53:06,423 --> 00:53:10,186
I was going to teach her
a new knot when I saw her.

651
00:53:10,186 --> 00:53:13,283
We picked the wrong day, Master Im.

652
00:53:18,459 --> 00:53:21,725
Maybe I was a little too hard on her.

653
00:53:22,392 --> 00:53:24,795
She did a great job.

654
00:53:27,815 --> 00:53:30,799
Tell her I appreciate all her hard work.

655
00:53:30,799 --> 00:53:32,388
Of course.

656
00:53:36,522 --> 00:53:37,685
So...

657
00:53:37,685 --> 00:53:40,159
Could you take a look at the exhibit layout?

658
00:53:40,159 --> 00:53:42,072
- Sure.
- This way.

659
00:54:36,528 --> 00:54:39,706
You've lost a lot of weight.

660
00:54:39,706 --> 00:54:41,927
You've been through a lot, haven't you?

661
00:54:43,217 --> 00:54:44,940
I'm okay.

662
00:54:44,940 --> 00:54:49,719
I just feel awful for leaving the team
before the event.

663
00:54:50,729 --> 00:54:53,742
When are you coming back?

664
00:54:55,382 --> 00:54:58,133
How can I?

665
00:54:58,133 --> 00:55:02,933
People are still attacking APPELLO
because of me.

666
00:55:02,933 --> 00:55:06,853
Everyone knows now you're not a sasaeng fan.

667
00:55:08,673 --> 00:55:11,357
I've been thinking...

668
00:55:11,357 --> 00:55:16,310
Was my reason for joining APPELLO
really that innocent?

669
00:55:17,723 --> 00:55:20,510
Maybe it wasn't.

670
00:55:21,337 --> 00:55:27,750
Part of me thought I'd get to be closer to him.

671
00:55:31,356 --> 00:55:33,647
You probably wouldn't understand.

672
00:55:33,647 --> 00:55:35,921
Why wouldn't I?

673
00:55:35,921 --> 00:55:40,608
I understand you better than you think.

674
00:55:40,608 --> 00:55:44,743
Wanting to be closer to a star you love,

675
00:55:44,743 --> 00:55:47,716
wanting to do anything you can for them...

676
00:55:49,476 --> 00:55:51,120
Actually...

677
00:55:51,120 --> 00:55:53,926
I used to be a fan of Director Lee too.

678
00:55:56,337 --> 00:55:57,368
Sorry?

679
00:55:57,368 --> 00:55:59,514
You were?

680
00:56:00,814 --> 00:56:04,728
I was the first president of D-Angel.

681
00:56:04,728 --> 00:56:06,321
What?

682
00:56:10,501 --> 00:56:13,087
Wait. Don't tell me...

683
00:56:31,507 --> 00:56:33,918
The antis who harassed DNX
when they first debuted...

684
00:56:33,918 --> 00:56:37,984
You took them on 17 to one and wiped them out.

685
00:56:37,984 --> 00:56:41,804
The legendary first D-Angel president?

686
00:56:43,017 --> 00:56:46,742
That was really you?

687
00:56:46,742 --> 00:56:48,631
It wasn't 17 to one.

688
00:56:48,631 --> 00:56:50,711
It was 19 to one.

689
00:56:55,748 --> 00:56:59,921
You practically created
D-Angel fan culture after that.

690
00:57:01,847 --> 00:57:05,261
So how did you end up at APPELLO?

691
00:57:06,853 --> 00:57:11,490
When Director Lee started his boutique,
he reached out to me first.

692
00:57:11,490 --> 00:57:14,579
I was working for a fashion company then.

693
00:57:16,769 --> 00:57:21,519
I had my own motives at first too.

694
00:57:21,519 --> 00:57:25,303
Getting to work with a star you admire...

695
00:57:25,303 --> 00:57:28,188
that feels like a dream for a fan.

696
00:57:28,188 --> 00:57:32,498
When they succeed,
it almost feels like you did too.

697
00:57:33,431 --> 00:57:37,716
But after a while, I realized something.

698
00:57:37,716 --> 00:57:42,878
What really matters is who I am.

699
00:57:43,779 --> 00:57:50,256
What I enjoy most,
and what I want to be good at.

700
00:57:50,256 --> 00:57:55,692
I think you've asked yourself the same things.

701
00:57:58,955 --> 00:58:01,421
So, Da Reum.

702
00:58:02,367 --> 00:58:04,306
Come back to work.

703
00:58:04,306 --> 00:58:07,166
Why run away when you did nothing wrong?

704
00:58:07,166 --> 00:58:10,924
No one cares more or works harder than you.

705
00:58:10,924 --> 00:58:16,133
We're all waiting for you to come back.

706
00:58:23,329 --> 00:58:25,020
Actually...

707
00:58:25,020 --> 00:58:27,322
I want to go back too.

708
00:58:28,023 --> 00:58:32,562
But if I do, it'll only make things harder
for CEO Kang.

709
00:58:33,956 --> 00:58:35,923
You haven't seen it yet?

710
00:58:36,520 --> 00:58:38,544
Seen what?

711
00:58:38,544 --> 00:58:41,681
He posted APPELLO's official statement.

712
00:58:42,685 --> 00:58:44,032
Really?

713
00:58:47,104 --> 00:58:51,397
<i>Actually, CEO Kang asked me to come.</i>

714
00:58:53,177 --> 00:58:55,547
<i>He wanted me to give you this knot.</i>

715
00:58:55,547 --> 00:59:00,453
<i>He's been really worried about you.</i>

716
00:59:10,931 --> 00:59:11,961
[APPELLO]

717
00:59:11,961 --> 00:59:13,437
[APPELLO Official Statement]

718
00:59:14,068 --> 00:59:18,246
<i>APPELLO has reviewed the facts
regarding the recent allegations</i>

719
00:59:18,246 --> 00:59:21,122
<i>involving one of our employees,</i>

720
00:59:21,122 --> 00:59:25,535
<i>and confirmed that she is not a sasaeng fan.</i>

721
00:59:30,902 --> 00:59:34,405
<i>She has, in fact, remained dedicated
to her work</i>

722
00:59:34,405 --> 00:59:38,444
<i>and carried out her duties
with diligence and integrity.</i>

723
00:59:52,743 --> 00:59:56,800
<i>Despite this, some fans
continue to spread false claims</i>

724
00:59:56,800 --> 00:59:59,534
<i>and pressure her to resign.</i>

725
00:59:59,534 --> 01:00:01,841
- I knew he'd handle it.
- Yeah?

726
01:00:01,841 --> 01:00:04,006
Hey! Just listen.

727
01:00:04,006 --> 01:00:07,346
<i>APPELLO will not give in
to unreasonable demands.</i>

728
01:00:07,346 --> 01:00:09,810
<i>Nor will we tolerate
any further harassment or threats</i>

729
01:00:09,810 --> 01:00:12,062
<i>against our employees.</i>

730
01:00:12,062 --> 01:00:13,919
[APPELLO's CEO handled this perfectly]

731
01:00:13,919 --> 01:00:15,835
[That poor rookie did nothing wrong]

732
01:00:15,835 --> 01:00:17,768
[Now THAT is real leadership]

733
01:00:21,176 --> 01:00:24,766
<i>She is, and will continue to be,</i>

734
01:00:24,766 --> 01:00:29,199
<i>a valued member of APPELLO.</i>

735
01:01:01,104 --> 01:01:02,759
Ms. Nam.

736
01:01:07,289 --> 01:01:09,439
What are you doing here this late?

737
01:01:14,084 --> 01:01:15,705
Did you run here?

738
01:01:18,530 --> 01:01:20,230
Yes.

739
01:01:22,050 --> 01:01:24,119
It's freezing out.

740
01:01:41,457 --> 01:01:43,323
Sir.

741
01:01:43,323 --> 01:01:47,369
I don't want to quit.

742
01:01:52,776 --> 01:01:55,556
Then why did you resign?

743
01:01:58,483 --> 01:02:00,541
Because of you.

744
01:02:02,402 --> 01:02:05,660
You kept making me work
even when I wasn't at the office.

745
01:02:05,660 --> 01:02:08,286
I can't just let that slide.

746
01:02:10,829 --> 01:02:17,423
You said I am, and will continue to be,
an APPELLO employee.

747
01:02:22,251 --> 01:02:24,431
That official statement...

748
01:02:27,257 --> 01:02:29,134
I'm sorry it took so long.

749
01:02:31,518 --> 01:02:35,977
You believed in me,
so I'll give APPELLO my best.

750
01:02:40,571 --> 01:02:46,457
As CEO, I have to think twice
before every decision.

751
01:02:48,984 --> 01:02:51,883
I overthink things.

752
01:02:51,883 --> 01:02:53,494
I hesitate.

753
01:02:55,651 --> 01:02:58,064
I'm not as brave as I seem.

754
01:03:01,313 --> 01:03:06,012
You've been through a lot, haven't you?

755
01:03:08,526 --> 01:03:10,095
No.

756
01:03:10,763 --> 01:03:14,226
I'm the one who's sorry.

757
01:03:16,019 --> 01:03:20,730
From now on, I'm done hiding how I feel.

758
01:03:20,730 --> 01:03:23,030
I'm going to be honest about everything.

759
01:03:23,030 --> 01:03:25,387
No more saying,

760
01:03:25,387 --> 01:03:30,267
"I won't resent you if you fire me,"
or "I'm fine."

761
01:03:32,488 --> 01:03:34,759
I missed APPELLO.

762
01:03:34,759 --> 01:03:38,185
I missed my work so much.

763
01:03:40,911 --> 01:03:42,911
And...

764
01:03:44,498 --> 01:03:46,457
And...

765
01:03:53,144 --> 01:03:56,443
I missed you, sir.

766
01:04:03,977 --> 01:04:05,977
I mean...

767
01:04:07,411 --> 01:04:09,224
I...

768
01:04:10,062 --> 01:04:13,570
I think I love you.

769
01:05:35,589 --> 01:05:37,662
[#Epilogue]
"Being a sasaeng and getting paid?"

770
01:05:37,662 --> 01:05:40,135
"Must be nice."

771
01:05:41,459 --> 01:05:44,156
Hey. What about this one?

772
01:05:44,156 --> 01:05:47,526
Yeah, this could violate
both the Network Act and the Criminal Act.

773
01:05:47,526 --> 01:05:48,936
First, get the post taken down.

774
01:05:48,936 --> 01:05:52,022
We'll need a warrant to identify the user.

775
01:05:52,022 --> 01:05:54,307
Got screenshots of everything.

776
01:05:54,307 --> 01:05:55,860
Good.

777
01:05:55,860 --> 01:05:58,857
[Celebrity Community]
Once we send the platform an official request,

778
01:05:58,857 --> 01:06:01,206
the posts should be down by tonight.

779
01:06:01,206 --> 01:06:02,816
Okay.

780
01:06:02,816 --> 01:06:06,242
"A company that hires a stalker
deserves to go under."

781
01:06:07,299 --> 01:06:08,849
Screenshot that too!

782
01:06:08,849 --> 01:06:10,008
Okay.

783
01:06:11,404 --> 01:06:15,999
"What if Lee Chan's being gaslit
by that sasaeng?"

784
01:06:17,640 --> 01:06:19,986
Damn. Report it.

785
01:06:21,410 --> 01:06:24,781
"Honestly, I'm kind of jealous of her."

786
